          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Using OpenMP parallel for with static scheduling on the outer loop over groups, each thread maintains its own local sorted list of k nearest neighbors (allocated once outside the parallel region). After the parallel region, per-thread lists are merged in order of increasing thread ID to preserve input-order tie-breaking. Static scheduling assigns contiguous group chunks deterministically, and merging by thread order ensures that points from earlier groups are inserted into the global top-k list before later groups, matching the sequential insertion behavior for equal distances. This reduces synchronization overhead compared to critical sections while exploiting work sharing and static scheduling for deterministic chunk assignment.",
