          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Flatten all points into three contiguous arrays (xs, ys, labels) during input parsing to maximize spatial locality and enable sequential memory access in the distance computation loop. Use a stack-allocated top-k list with linear insertion sort (O(k) per point, k ≤ 256) to avoid heap allocation overhead and maintain sorted order efficiently. Replace qsort+scan with a frequency histogram over 256 possible character values to eliminate sorting entirely while preserving tie-breaking by smallest character. This combination minimizes cache misses, reduces dynamic instructions, and improves overall memory locality.",
          "id": "2055e7a84d1542af",
          "ordinal": 19,
          "parent_id": null,
          "role": "A",
