          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Flattening the matrix into a 1D array improves spatial locality for sequential access. Using an integral image (summed-area table) reduces submatrix sum computation to O(1), lowering overall complexity from O(S N^2) to O(N^2). This transformation also enables fully row-major memory accesses, improving cache utilization.",
          "id": "a69e622158bd4a3d",
