          "hypothesis": "Converting to explicit struct-of-arrays (SoA) layout with aligned allocation, restrict qualifiers, hoisting p[i] reads outside the inner loop, and applying #pragma omp simd reduction on force accumulation enables efficient SIMD vectorization (NEON) while retaining OpenMP thread-level parallelism. This reduces memory traffic per iteration and allows the compiler to generate wider vector instructions, lowering execution time below previous SoA-based results.",
