          "delegation_parent": "R/A",
          "depth": 2,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Once the max-heap is full, most points are rejected because their squared distance already exceeds the current k-th largest distance. Since d = dx^2 + dy^2 >= dx^2 in floating point for finite inputs, checking only the x-component first avoids computing and adding the y-component for clearly non-qualifying points. Keeping the current heap maximum in a local register also removes repeated root loads from memory while preserving sequential AoS traversal of each group's points for spatial locality.",
