          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Using NEON SIMD intrinsics (vld2q_f32) to compute squared Euclidean distances for four points at a time improves memory-level parallelism and vectorization on ARM64, reducing the dominant distance-computation cost while preserving exact floating-point results and tie-breaking semantics; this should outperform scalar baseline.",
