          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Streaming the matrix row-by-row into a flat ring buffer of only S rows, maintaining vertical column sums for the current S-row window, and scanning horizontal windows over that contiguous colSum array replaces the snake traversal's O(S*N^2) strided memory accesses with O(N^2) sequential streaming accesses. This improves cache locality and reduces memory traffic while keeping intermediate sliding-window values within 32-bit range on valid inputs.",
