        "mission": {
          "base_commit": "4264e6b9f38a7e19daeab1f48c84c307b185f7fb",
          "delegation_parent": "R/B",
          "depth": 2,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Replace the O(S*N^2) per-column sliding-window algorithm with an O(N^2) vertical column-sum approach. A running sum of each column over S rows is maintained and updated by adding/subtracting whole rows; for every starting row a horizontal slide scans all columns in O(N). The independent column updates are explicitly vectorized with OpenMP SIMD, while the only sequential dependency (the horizontal accumulator) remains local to one row. This drastically reduces arithmetic and memory traffic versus the original per-column S-element update loop.",
          "id": "fe369837c49d4785",
          "ordinal": 15,
          "parent_id": "8799e4babe044c8d",
          "role": "B",
          "source_commits": [],
          "sources": [],
          "transformations": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Flattened matrix storage to a single std::vector<int> for improved locality and SIMD alignment.",
              "Replaced the per-column sliding-window (which did S-element updates for each row shift) with a running column-sum vector that is updated by adding one whole row and removing another, reducing update cost from O(S*N^2) to O(N^2).",
              "Added explicit #pragma omp simd on all independent column loops: initial column-sum accumulation and the vertical window update.",
              "Kept the horizontal scan as a simple sequential sliding loop because it carries a dependency; its total work is only O(N) per starting row."
            ]
          },
