          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Combining structure-of-arrays (SoA) layout with cache blocking over the i-loop and OpenMP parallelization over tiles reduces main-memory traffic from O(N^2) to O(N^2/TILE) while preserving each body's exact sequential j-summation order. Each thread processes a contiguous tile of bodies, reading every other body once per tile; this improves memory locality and should outperform the previous SoA+OpenMP version.",
