          "depth": 2,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Converting the body data from Array-of-Structs to Struct-of-Arrays and using OpenMP's combined parallel-for-SIMD construct on both the force loop (across bodies) and the position-update loop lets each thread process multiple bodies in SIMD lanes while keeping every body's inner j-reduction scalar. This preserves exact floating-point results per body, adds data-level parallelism beyond the existing 4-thread speedup, and improves memory locality for vector loads.",
